# Agent scratch output.
#
# The leaf's agent runtime writes per-step records to `debug/turn-debug/`
# relative to the PROJECT ROOT. Inside the driving guest the project
# root IS this checkout, and the ship step stages with `git add -A` --
# so without this rule every automated PR carries a pile of machine
# scratch alongside the actual edit. Three such files were committed to
# `main` before this rule existed.
#
# These are a byproduct of HOW an edit was produced, never part of the
# edit itself. `scripts/check-no-scratch.sh` asserts this rule holds.
debug/turn-debug/
